  "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#semiotic_projection_2",
  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_2",
  "label": "User projected onto the target of the frustration (the reporting system or audience)",
  "description": "The user is also projected onto the implied 'you' in the text ('i don't need you to tell me...'). The user sees themselves as the meme creator, and the 'you' represents the audience, moderators, or social media platforms that are reporting their content. The aggressive pointing gesture of the man visually directs the blame or frustration towards this 'you'. The user is projecting their own frustration at the reporting system onto the visual of the man pointing, which symbolizes the external force causing the reports.",
